* the existing char/ probe commands bind unchanged.
*
* HARNESS.  The layout cell generates its bias legs INTERNALLY off pbias:
* XLR1 (nb0), XLPA (nv, 936 nA), XLPB_LVR (nvb ref, 1394 nA), XLO2 (nsv),
* XLO3 (out).  Drive ONLY supplies, vrefb, ve, pbias, u and v -- injecting
* any of those legs a second time doubles it.  See char/eml_ln_accuracy.spice.
*
* THE ln ARGUMENT IS NOT v.  XLPA puts a fixed 936 nA (1.872 units) on the
* nv transdiode and the reference leg XLPB_LVR is 1394 nA (2.789 units), so
* the cell computes ln((v + 1.87)/2.79) -- the documented 2-unit pedestal
* (README: "ln input becomes ln((v+2)/3)").  A raw a + k*ln(v) fit of this
